},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T04:11:32-07:00","id":1515340,"title":"","content":"This could certainly be a creation myth that would fit in Exalted quite nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T20:53:47-07:00","id":1515443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1515319-origins-of-humanity-and-gods-in-exalted?p=1515340#post1515340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could certainly be a creation myth that would fit in Exalted quite nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. For every bit of worldbuiling, there's some peculiar bit of regional folklore or reinterpretation of more mainstream religions and philosophies in idiosyncratic ways. One might even dare say the Immaculate Faith is an extremely successful example of such &quot;revisionist cosmologies&quot; turned mainstream itself by sheer raw force. So agreed, the clip's narrative could fit right in amidst Creation well enough, even if not wholy - or at all - true to how the setting portrays the history of primordials, gods and humanity among the mortal races.<br /> <br /> In fact there's one character and race of beings - Zicnal and his people, the Asmani giants that, according to a legend, when the ancients shaped Creation, were set to hold up the corners of the sky, as described in Thousand Devils Night Parade - that might fit right in, even though they might deny such a tale themselves if asked (or not, who knows what sort of individual ideas and agendas one might develop amidst the chaos-drenced borders between reality and surreality they have taken to inhabit in the Age of Sorrows).\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T00:05:12-07:00","id":1515445,"title":"","content":"I would just like to point out that this song is basically retelling the myth told by Aristophanes in the Symposium, which I've always found to be an interesting little story. It's a classical myth that wouldn't really be out of place in Exalted's world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T06:33:39-07:00","id":1515455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1515319-origins-of-humanity-and-gods-in-exalted?p=1515445#post1515445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just like to point out that this song is basically retelling the myth told by Aristophanes in the Symposium, which I've always found to be an interesting little story. It's a classical myth that wouldn't really be out of place in Exalted's world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it ressonates with the concept of &quot;ages of humanity&quot; and races of man that bordered the gods in greatness and would be diminished by their intervention or continued human strife through the ages, a theme that seems very dear on a number of variants to greek literature and phylosophy in particular. In Creation the Jadeborn - and maybe the Lintha - could be sources of fodder to inspire this kind of narrative.<br /> <br /> (Though the Lintha in particular, through their connection with Kimbery, have as much or more of &quot;a people their own, that blends the human and supernatural&quot;, akin to Khmer legendry relating their origin as people to nagas or serpent deities, i guess)<br /> <br /> Anyway, tribes, city-states, nations or even whole regions/subcontinents having their own peculiar alt-story/myths deviating from the general lore, and that occasionally might even have some peculiar hidden kernel of truth to the case of the teller, is certainly something that fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-18-2023, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}